{
  "analysis": "Market reading: the session after the last close shows a broad 1-day rebound (most assets +0.3% to +1.9%), but the 5d and 20d windows are still negative for most risk assets, so this looks like a bounce inside a mild downtrend rather than a confirmed reversal. The portfolio is down only 1.62% from peak, so no drawdown restrictions apply. The reliable signal in the forecasts is interval width, not the median: A09 (bonds, 5d width 3.4%) and A02 (US broad, 3.9%) have by far the narrowest intervals, while the single stocks (A01, A07, A13, A14) and gold carry the widest intervals (8-12%) and the highest realized vol (26-44%). Main risks: (1) over-concentration in defensive assets — cash 19.9% plus bonds 21.0% is ~41% of the portfolio, a large opportunity cost if the rebound extends; (2) high-vol single-stock exposure would add risk without forecast support; (3) group concentration if I add A10 on top of A02. Changes I am making: trim bonds modestly (still well above baseline) and gold, redeploy part of the cash into the three best risk-adjusted assets — A02 (narrowest equity interval, lowest vol), A06 (highest equity median with a relatively narrow interval, non-US diversification), and A03 (strongest 20d momentum) — keep all four weak single stocks at zero, and land cash at ~15.5%, comfortably above the 10% floor. All targets respect the 15pp-above-baseline increase cap, the 25%/10%/30% caps, and group limits.",
  "positions": [
    {
      "symbol": "A02",
      "target_weight": 0.17,
      "rationale": "Increase from 13.6% to 17% (+7.7pp vs baseline, within the 15pp cap): narrowest 5d interval among equities (3.9%), lowest vol (8.7%), positive median, and the natural core US equity holding into a rebound. Group us_broad stays at 17% with A10 at zero.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    },
    {
      "symbol": "A11",
      "target_weight": 0.06,
      "rationale": "Hold near baseline (6.0% vs 6.97% baseline, current 5.98%): moderate interval width (5.2%) and vol 12.7%; no concrete edge to deviate in either direction.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "symbol": "A10",
      "target_weight": 0.0,
      "rationale": "Keep at zero (-6.4pp vs baseline): same us_broad group as A02, which dominates on lower vol (8.7% vs 13.0%), narrower interval (3.9% vs 5.6%) and better 20d trend (-1.7% vs -4.8%); avoid duplicating group exposure.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    },
    {
      "symbol": "A06",
      "target_weight": 0.10,
      "rationale": "Increase from 8.0% to 10.0% (+1.8pp vs baseline): highest 5d median among equity ETFs (+0.15%) with the second-narrowest interval (4.4%) and moderate vol (10.6%); adds developed ex-US diversification.",
      "confidence": 0.54
    },
    {
      "symbol": "A12",
      "target_weight": 0.045,
      "rationale": "Hold near baseline (4.5% vs 4.83%): positive 5d/20d momentum (+0.5%/+1.7%) but the highest ETF vol (19.7%) and a wide interval (7.5%) justify keeping the position small.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "symbol": "A03",
      "target_weight": 0.06,
      "rationale": "Increase from 3.5% to 6.0% (+0.9pp vs baseline): strongest 20d momentum among ETFs (+6.7%) with a positive median; sized modestly because the interval is wide (7.1%) and vol is 15.5%.",
      "confidence": 0.53
    },
    {
      "symbol": "A04",
      "target_weight": 0.06,
      "rationale": "Hold near baseline (6.0% vs 6.2%): high vol (20.5%) and a flat median give no reason to deviate; health exposure is adequate.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "symbol": "A08",
      "target_weight": 0.078,
      "rationale": "Hold at baseline (7.8%): narrow interval (4.7%) and median ~0; steady financials ETF exposure alongside stock A15 (group total 13.5%, well under the 30% cap).",
      "confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "symbol": "A09",
      "target_weight": 0.18,
      "rationale": "Trim from 21.0% to 18.0% (still +7.5pp vs baseline, within the 15pp cap and 25% ETF cap): narrowest interval overall (3.4%) and highest median (+0.32%) make it the defensive anchor, but with cash already near 20% the combined defensive weight is excessive; the small trim funds higher-conviction equity adds while cash stays above 15%.",
      "confidence": 0.53
    },
    {
      "symbol": "A05",
      "target_weight": 0.035,
      "rationale": "Trim from 4.2% to 3.5% (-0.9pp vs baseline): highest vol (27.9%) and widest interval (8.3%) in the universe; its diversification role is already covered by bonds and cash.",
      "confidence": 0.52
    },
    {
      "symbol": "A01",
      "target_weight": 0.0,
      "rationale": "Keep at zero (-3.1pp vs baseline): extreme vol (43.7%) and the widest 5d interval (11.8%); no forecast support for initiating a single-stock tech position.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    },
    {
      "symbol": "A15",
      "target_weight": 0.0573,
      "rationale": "Hold exactly at baseline (5.73%): moderate interval (6.3%) and vol (14.5%); the only single stock currently held, and there is no data-driven reason to change it.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "symbol": "A13",
      "target_weight": 0.0,
      "rationale": "Keep at zero (-4.2pp vs baseline): despite positive 20d momentum (+5.3%), vol is 23.1% and the interval is wide (8.7%); prefer gaining energy exposure through ETF A03 (lower vol, narrower interval).",
      "confidence": 0.53
    },
    {
      "symbol": "A07",
      "target_weight": 0.0,
      "rationale": "Keep at zero (-3.6pp vs baseline): worst 20d trend (-7.6%), negative median (-0.71%), vol 29.9% and wide interval (10.1%); clear avoid.",
      "confidence": 0.55
